# React UI

- Renderer must not access Node, FS, or shell directly — use preload API only.
- No hard-coded user-visible strings; use localization keys (pl/uk/en).
- Every control needs an accessible label; do not communicate status by color alone.
- Keep the Password Remover screen focused: queue, password, output, progress, results.
- Prefer existing `packages/ui` components before inventing new primitives.
- Long work stays off the renderer thread (main/engine handles PDF work).
